! Paper

Settings for the Paper theme.

!! Layout

<$radio tiddler="$:/themes/BurningTreeC/vanilla-paper/options/sidebarlayout" value="fluid-fixed"> Fluid story river, fixed sidebar</$radio>

<$radio tiddler="$:/themes/BurningTreeC/vanilla-paper/options/sidebarlayout" value="fixed-fluid"> Fixed story river, fluid sidebar</$radio>

> In ''fixed-fluid'' the story river keeps its width, so hiding the sidebar is composited entirely on the GPU — nothing reflows. In ''fluid-fixed'' the river reclaims the freed space, which is a layout change by definition; it is interpolated rather than snapped, so it glides, but it is not GPU work.

<$checkbox tiddler="$:/themes/BurningTreeC/vanilla-paper/options/fullwidth" field="text" checked="yes" unchecked="no" default="no"> Full width — story river and tiddlers take all the space the sidebar is not using</$checkbox>

> Full width lifts the cap on tiddler width and the 68-character measure on tiddler text, so tiddlers fill the story river. The sidebar keeps the sizing its layout mode gives it. In ''fluid-fixed'' the river takes the viewport minus the fixed sidebar. In ''fixed-fluid'' the sidebar is fluid and owns the space beside the river while it is visible, so the river only expands to the full viewport once the sidebar is hidden. On a wide display full width means lines longer than is comfortable to read, which is why it is off by default.

!! Paper

<$checkbox tiddler="$:/themes/BurningTreeC/vanilla-paper/options/marginrule" field="text" checked="yes" unchecked="no" default="yes"> Draw the margin rule down each tiddler</$checkbox>

<$checkbox tiddler="$:/themes/BurningTreeC/vanilla-paper/options/ruleseditor" field="text" checked="yes" unchecked="no" default="yes"> Rule the editor like ruled paper</$checkbox>

<$checkbox tiddler="$:/themes/BurningTreeC/vanilla-paper/options/stickytitles" field="text" checked="yes" unchecked="no" default="no"> Keep tiddler titles visible while scrolling</$checkbox>

!! Sidebar

<$radio tiddler="$:/themes/BurningTreeC/vanilla-paper/options/sidebarside" value="end"> Sidebar on the trailing edge</$radio>

<$radio tiddler="$:/themes/BurningTreeC/vanilla-paper/options/sidebarside" value="start"> Sidebar on the leading edge</$radio>

> Leading and trailing rather than left and right, because the layout is written with logical properties: in a left-to-right wiki the trailing edge is the right, in a right-to-left wiki it is the left. The slide direction follows, so the sidebar always leaves toward the edge it is anchored to.

!! Controls

<$checkbox tiddler="$:/themes/BurningTreeC/vanilla-paper/options/toolbaralways" field="text" checked="yes" unchecked="no" default="no"> Keep tiddler toolbars visible instead of revealing them on hover</$checkbox>

<$checkbox tiddler="$:/themes/BurningTreeC/vanilla-paper/options/toolbarhover" field="text" checked="yes" unchecked="no" default="yes"> Draw a background behind toolbar buttons on hover</$checkbox>

<$checkbox tiddler="$:/themes/BurningTreeC/vanilla-paper/options/pressanimation" field="text" checked="yes" unchecked="no" default="yes"> Let buttons and tag pills move when pressed</$checkbox>

> The press movement is a single pixel downwards on `:active` and nothing else. It is switched off automatically for anyone whose system asks for reduced motion; this setting is for turning it off without that.

